# 3. `mode: "lexical"` DEMANDÉ : pas de `note`. Il n'y a rien à expliquer — le
#    client a eu ce qu'il voulait. Un filtre qui ne correspond à aucune racine
#    rend zéro hit, pas une erreur.
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"fouine_search","arguments":{"query":"electrolyse","mode":"lexical","folder":"Cours"}}}
< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<any>"}],"structuredContent":{"hits":[],"total_pages":0,"total_docs":0,"totals_approximate":false,"mode_used":"lexical","semantic_available":false,"semantic_coverage_pct":0,"semantic_stats":null,"semantic_rank_scale":null,"note":null,"name_matches":[],"fuzzy_fallback":false,"quorum":false,"hybrid_disarmed":null,"has_more":false,"next_cursor":null,"elapsed_ms":"<any>","documents":{},"facets":null,"fuzzy_expanded":false,"semantic_scope":{"filtered":false,"pages":6,"vectorised":0}}}}

# 4. `doc_ids` — « rechercher dans les résultats ». Les totaux suivent le
#    filtre : 3 pages dans 1 document, pas 6 dans 2.
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":5,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"fouine_search","arguments":{"query":"electrolyse","doc_ids":[2],"limit":1}}}
< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":5,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<any>"}],"structuredContent":{"hits":[{"doc_id":2,"page":1,"path":"Users/essai/Livres/document-2.pdf","abs_path":null,"link":"fouine://open?doc=2&page=1","folder":"Livres","ext":"pdf","snippet":"«electrolyse» enthalpie page 1 du document 2","bm25":0,"source":"native","engine":"none","fuzzy_distance":0,"semantic_only":false,"why":{"kind":"exact","terms_found":["electrolyse"]},"embedded_image":null,"relevance_pct":100,"slide":null,"time_seconds":null}],"total_pages":3,"total_docs":1,"totals_approximate":false,"mode_used":"lexical","semantic_available":false,"semantic_coverage_pct":0,"semantic_stats":null,"semantic_rank_scale":null,"note":"semantic model not installed — lexical only (`fouine model download` installs it)","name_matches":[],"fuzzy_fallback":false,"quorum":false,"hybrid_disarmed":null,"has_more":true,"next_cursor":"eyJmIjoiOTk4ZmE5ZTcxOWQ1MDVlNWUxZGNmZGFjIiwibyI6MSwidiI6MX0","elapsed_ms":"<any>","documents":{},"facets":null,"fuzzy_expanded":false,"semantic_scope":{"filtered":false,"pages":6,"vectorised":0}}}}

# 5. Une requête que l'analyseur refuse est une erreur d'OUTIL (`isError`), avec
#    le message ANGLAIS de `QueryError` — le même que la CLI, qui sort en 64.
#    L'argument est une chaîne valide : c'est son CONTENU que le modèle doit
#    réécrire, et un `isError` porte la phrase là où il la lit (audit A1m-07).
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":6,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"fouine_search","arguments":{"query":"-electrolyse"}}}
< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":6,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<any>"}],"isError":true}}

# 5 bis. `AND`, `OR`, `NOT` en majuscules : les mots-clés de FTS5. Ils vidaient
#    le SQL de la requête interne et sortaient en 3 côté CLI (A1m-07).
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":16,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"fouine_search","arguments":{"query":"electrolyse OR enthalpie"}}}
< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":16,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<any>"}],"isError":true}}

# 6. Un jeton qui n'est pas un curseur de ce serveur.
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":7,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"fouine_search","arguments":{"query":"electrolyse","cursor":"pas-un-curseur"}}}
< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":7,"error":{"code":-32602,"message":"Invalid params: cursor is not a cursor produced by this server","data":{"reason":"cursor is not a cursor produced by this server"}}}

# 7. LE CAS QUI COMPTE : un curseur VALIDE, mais produit par une AUTRE requête.
#    Sans ce refus, le client obtiendrait la page 2 d'une recherche appliquée
#    aux résultats d'une autre — des trous et des doublons, sans un mot.
> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":8,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"fouine_search","arguments":{"query":"enthalpie","limit":2,"cursor":"eyJmIjoiMGExZjEzY2Q5NTc1YmFlNWQ2YzliZjcwIiwibyI6MiwidiI6MX0"}}}
< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":8,"error":{"code":-32602,"message":"Invalid params: cursor does not match these arguments","data":{"reason":"cursor does not match these arguments"}}}
